{
  "id": "inhibitory-conditioning",
  "term": "inhibitory conditioning",
  "definition": "Inhibitory conditioning is a form of associative learning in which a cue comes to signal that an expected outcome will not happen. For example, when one stimulus usually predicts an event, adding another stimulus during trials without that event can teach that the added cue means the outcome will be omitted.",
